<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n38983" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">prō-rīto</span></b> ,
		āre, v. a.
		like ir-rito, āre; cf. also ira. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>To provoke</i>, <i>cause</i>, or <i>produce by irritation</i> (post - Aug.), <i><span class="en">Plin. 26, 8,
				58, § 90</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>, <i>to incite</i>, <i>entice</i>, <i>allure</i>, <i>tempt</i> (post-Aug.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">nisi pretium proritat,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Col.
					2, 10, 17</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">quem spes proritat,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sen. Ep. 23, 2</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">proritat illos rei species,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. Tranq. 12, 5</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">stomachum varietate aptā ciborum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Scrib. Comp. 104</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">aliquem ad furias,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Arn. 5, 178</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
